ADVERSARIAL BOUNDARY COVERAGE
- A boundary-independent username/password detector sanitizes embedded malformed authorities even when their separator is also legal in a username.
- Direct redaction, DatabaseLifecycle errors, and real argparse diagnostics cover whitespace, comma, semicolon, slash, hyphen, plus, dot, underscore, tilde, percent, and colon joins.
- First-pass and repeated redaction retain the `db-reset:` and `kl db-reset: error: unrecognized arguments:` diagnostic prefixes.
- The detector requires a non-whitespace password start, preventing a colon-terminated safe prefix followed by prose from being consumed as credentials.
- All earlier configuration, serialization, URL, parser, fixture, DB/CLI, host, mapping, set, exception, format, delimiter, encoding, subclass, cycle/depth, and non-mutation probes remain covered.
